### Validate configuration with Zod in ConfigModule

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/migration.md

Pass a Standard Schema-compatible validation schema, such as Zod, directly to `validationSchema` in `ConfigModule.forRoot()`. Modern Standard Schema libraries are recommended over legacy Joi validation for new projects.

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

ConfigModule.forRoot({
  validationSchema: z.object({
    NODE_ENV: z
      .enum(['development', 'production', 'test', 'provision'])
      .default('development'),
    PORT: z.coerce.number().default(3000),
  }),
});
```

