### Define a Zod validationSchema in ConfigModule.forRoot()

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/docs.nestjs.com/blob/master/content/application/configuration.md

Pass a Standard Schema-compatible schema through the validationSchema property of the options object passed to forRoot(). Defaults are applied when NODE_ENV and PORT are not provided; leaving a variable without a default makes it required and throws during bootstrap if missing. PORT uses z.coerce.number() because environment variables always arrive as strings.

```typescript
@@filename(app.module)
import { z } from 'zod';

@Module({
  imports: [
    ConfigModule.forRoot({
      validationSchema: z.object({
        NODE_ENV: z
          .enum(['development', 'production', 'test', 'provision'])
          .default('development'),
        PORT: z.coerce.number().default(3000),
      }),
    }),
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

